<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<span data-teams="true"><p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">CLIENT CONTACT NAME</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">,</span></p></span><div style=""><font face="arial"><br>As 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_ </span>comes to an end, there are several important things to keep in mind regarding your Insperity payroll and benefits. Please feel free to share the reminders below with your employees as needed:</font></div><div style=""><ul><li><font face="arial"><b>Is the address and email on file with Insperity current?</b> Outdated contact information could prevent you from receiving ID cards, your W-2, or other important communications. Visit "<a href="https://portalapps.insperity.com/MyProfile/">My Profile</a>" on Insperity Premier(TM) to view and update your contact information.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>If you'd prefer an electronic copy of your W-2, <a href="https://portal.insperity.com/pcms/w2_wage_and_tax_statement">opt in</a> on Insperity Premier by Dec. 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span></b>. Electronic W-2s will be available by Jan. 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b><font color="#ff0000">Open Enrollment for the Insperity Health Care Flexible Spending Account Plan (FSA) ends Dec. 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span></font></b>. For Plan Year 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>, you can elect $20 to $275.00 in monthly contributions, up to a maximum annual contribution of $3,300. Please <a href="https://portal.insperity.com/pcms/benefits">make your elections</a> by 11:59 p.m. Central Time on Dec. 31 if you wish to participate in 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>Have more than $500 of 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span> funds left in your Insperity Health Care FSA? You can roll over up to $500 into 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span> if you continue participating in the Insperity Health Care FSA, but any excess must be used by Dec. 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>, or you'll lose it!</b> You can visit the <a href="https://store.optum.com/">Optum Store</a> to purchase FSA-eligible products online if you need to spend down your remaining balance. You can also file claims through March 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">_</span>, for any eligible expenses you incur through Dec. 31, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>Need to make or change an HSA contribution election for Tax Year 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">_</span>?</b> Log in to <a href="https://portal.insperity.com/pcms/benefits">Insperity Premier</a> to change your election for 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span> after your last pay date of December. If you want an HSA election to take effect on your first pay date in 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span>, you'll need to make the election after your last pay date in December, but at least five days before your first pay date in January. As a reminder, 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);">_</span> HSA contribution limits are $4,300 for employee-only coverage, and $8550 for family coverage. Employees who turn 55 or older within the tax year may contribute an additional $1,000 of catchup contributions.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>The plan year for the Insperity Group Health Plan is the calendar year</b>. The plan year is based on a 12-month coverage period which begins Jan. 1 and ends Dec. 31. Your Insperity Group Health Plan deductible and out-of-pocket maximums will reset on Jan. 1, and generally, any plan design changes outlined in the Summary of Material Modifications for that plan year will take effect, even if your client company's enrollment and coverage periods do not follow the calendar year.</font></li><li><font face="arial">Refill your eligible prescriptions before your deductible resets on Jan. 1! Some coverage options under the Insperity Group Health Plan, including non-HDHP UnitedHealthcare Choice Plus options, have a separate pharmacy deductible that must be met before copays apply. Log in to <a href="https://portal.insperity.com/pcms/benefits">Insperity Premier</a> to view your coverage details.</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>Insperity is closed Dec. 25 and Jan. 1 for the holidays, and the Insperity Contact Center will be unavailable on those dates.</b></font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>Dec.<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);"> __</span>is the last day to process wages for 202<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">_</span></b>. Insperity Payroll Operations will be available on Dec. <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 51);">__</span> for client support and year-end payroll processing needs.&nbsp;</font></li><li><font face="arial"><b>Questions about your Insperity payroll or benefits?&nbsp;</b></font><span data-teams="true">For assistance, contact the Insperity Contact Center at 866.715.3552, 7am to 7pm Central time, Monday to Friday.</span></li></ul></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>